              "text": "stilus is probably inherited, from a Proto-Indo-European root steyg-, \"to prick, to pierce\" (EtymDB 2.1); English stick is a cousin (Lewis & Short). The spelling with y came later, from a mistaken link with Greek stylos, \"pillar\"."
